# Detection: Privilege Escalation via Group Membership Change

## Detection Name

Local Group Membership Added - Event ID 4732

## Description

This detection monitors for users being added to privileged local groups, such as Administrators or Workstations_LocalAdmins. Unauthorized group membership changes may indicate privilege escalation activity.

## Data Source

- Windows Security Event Log
- Event ID: 4732
- Sourcetype: WinEventLog:Security

## Detection Logic

Detect additions to privileged local groups.

## SPL Query

index=* sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4732
| search TargetUserName="Administrators" OR TargetUserName="Workstations_LocalAdmins"
| table _time, Account_Name, Member_Name, TargetUserName

## MITRE ATT&CK Mapping

- Tactic: Privilege Escalation (TA0004)
- Technique: Abuse Elevation Control Mechanism (T1548)

## Severity

Critical

## False Positives

- Authorized administrative changes
- IT maintenance activities
- Role updates during onboarding

## Tuning Considerations

- Whitelist known administrative accounts
- Alert only on non-IT_Helpdesk accounts
- Correlate with logon events (4624)

## Status

Active
